ik.fandom.com/wiki/Unnamed_Suit_042","status":"resolved","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A26469"},{"target_title":"Unnamed Suit 055","label":"Unnamed Suit 055","target_id":"huntik:page:26539","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Unnamed_Suit_055","status":"resolved","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A26539"}]},{"name":"height","value_wikitext":"8 feet 11 inches","value_text":"8 feet 11 inches","links":[]},{"name":"weight","value_wikitext":"610 pounds","value_text":"610 pounds","links":[]},{"name":"first","value_wikitext":"\"[[Home Turf]]\"","value_text":"\"Home Turf\"","links":[{"target_title":"Home Turf","label":"Home Turf","target_id":"huntik:page:3228","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Home_Turf","status":"resolved","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A3228"}]}],"start":0,"end":518}],"sections":[{"heading":"History","level":2,"wikitext":"Two Bonelasher Titans were summoned by [[The Professor's Personal Guard]] to fight [[Eathon Lambert]] in [[Atlantis]]. They were defeated by a combined attack from [[Dendras]] and [[Jirwolf]]. {{source|Coming of Age}}\n\nYears later, in [[Newgrange Passage Tomb]], Bonelasher was used by [[Klaus]]'s suits alongside [[Enforcer]]. One fought [[Caliban]] but was defeated. Later on, two defeated [[Lok Lambert]]'s [[Freelancer]] but were then taken out by [[Kilthane]] and [[Gybolg]]. {{Source|Home Turf}}\n\nBonelasher was used by [[Wilder]]'s Suits, alongside [[Venomaster]] and [[Gigadrone]] Titans, to pursue the Huntik team. One was defeated by being squashed under a tree levered by [[Dante Vale]]'s [[Dragonfist]] power. {{source|Knight of the Willblade}}","text":"Two Bonelasher Titans were summoned by The Professor's Personal Guard to fight Eathon Lambert in Atlantis. They were defeated by a combined attack from Dendras and Jirwolf. [Coming of Age]\n\nYears later, in Newgrange Passage Tomb, Bonelasher was used by Klaus's suits alongside Enforcer. One fought Caliban but was defeated. Later on, two defeated Lok Lambert's Freelancer but were then taken out by Kilthane and Gybolg. [Home Turf]\n\nBonelasher was used by Wilder's Suits, alongside Venomaster and Gigadrone Titans, to pursue the Huntik team. One was defeated by being squashed under a tree levered by Dante Vale's Dragonfist power. [Knight of the Willblade]"},{"heading":"Abilities","level":2,"wikitext":"Bonelasher can do massive amounts of damage with his fists. He is capable of punching through walls and Titans easily. He can stand amounts of damage most other Titans can't. With his razor-sharp claws and teeth, Bonelasher is best fought at a distance. Though Bonelasher is often paired with an [[Enforcer]] in battle, most of these Titans are preferred to be used independently.\n\n{{clear}}","text":"Bonelasher can do massive amounts of damage with his fists. He is capable of punching through walls and Titans easily. He can stand amounts of damage most other Titans can't. With his razor-sharp claws and teeth, Bonelasher is best fought at a distance. Though Bonelasher is often paired with an Enforcer in battle, most of these Titans are preferred to be used independently."},{"heading":"Gallery","level":2,"wikitext":"{{gallery}}\n<gallery position=\"center\" captionalign=\"center\">\nBonelasher Amulet.jpg|Bonelasher's Amulet\nBonelasher Icon.jpg|Bonelasher's Icon\nBonelasher.jpg|Bonelasher\n</gallery>","text":"Bonelasher Amulet.jpg|Bonelasher's Amulet\nBonelasher Icon.jpg|Bonelasher's Icon\nBonelasher.jpg|Bonelasher"},{"heading":"Trivia","level":2,"wikitext":"*Bonelasher was originally named '''Ribbed Gremlin''', revealed in the storyboard animatic of \"[[The Bookshop Hunter]]\", included on DVD Journal 4 – ''The Professor Revealed'' (Anime Works / US Release). In folklore, Gremlins were mischievous spirits known to cause trouble and complications in machinery.","text":"*Bonelasher was originally named Ribbed Gremlin, revealed in the storyboard animatic of \"The Bookshop Hunter\", included on DVD Journal 4 – The Professor Revealed (Anime Works / US Release). In folklore, Gremlins were mischievous spirits known to cause trouble and complications in machinery."},{"heading":"International Names","level":2,"wikitext":"{{InternationalNamesSmall\n|FR = Griffosaure}}\n\n[[Category:Titans]]\n[[Category:Swara-Titans]]\n[[Category:Warrior Titans]]\n[[Category:Organization Titans]]\n[[Category:Medium Titans]]\n[[Category:Season 1 Titans]]\n[[Category:Season 2 Titans]]\n{{clear}}{{SwaraBox}}","text":"French: Griffosaure"}],"full_text":"Bonelasher is the evolved cousin of Redcap, the favored Titan of low-level Organization Suits, but he is a bit stronger and harder to control. With the same aggression and passion for combat as his Titan relative, Bonelasher is best unleashed by his Seeker in the midst of a battle. With his army of razor-sharp claws and teeth, Bonelasher is best fought at distance.\n\n== History ==\nTwo Bonelasher Titans were summoned by The Professor's Personal Guard to fight Eathon Lambert in Atlantis. They were defeated by a combined attack from Dendras and Jirwolf. [Coming of Age]\n\nYears later, in Newgrange Passage Tomb, Bonelasher was used by Klaus's suits alongside Enforcer. One fought Caliban but was defeated. Later on, two defeated Lok Lambert's Freelancer but were then taken out by Kilthane and Gybolg. [Home Turf]\n\nBonelasher was used by Wilder's Suits, alongside Venomaster and Gigadrone Titans, to pursue the Huntik team. One was defeated by being squashed under a tree levered by Dante Vale's Dragonfist power. [Knight of the Willblade]\n\n== Abilities ==\nBonelasher can do massive amounts of damage with his fists. He is capable of punching through walls and Titans easily. He can stand amounts of damage most other Titans can't. With his razor-sharp claws and teeth, Bonelasher is best fought at a distance. Though Bonelasher is often paired with an Enforcer in battle, most of these Titans are preferred to be used independently.\n\n== Gallery ==\n\nBonelasher Amulet.jpg|Bonelasher's Amulet\nBonelasher Icon.jpg|Bonelasher's Icon\nBonelasher.jpg|Bonelasher\n\n== Trivia ==\n*Bonelasher was originally named Ribbed Gremlin, revealed in the storyboard animatic of \"The Bookshop Hunter\", included on DVD Journal 4 – The Professor Revealed (Anime Works / US Release). In folklore, Gremlins were mischievous spirits known to cause trouble and complications in machinery. \n\n== International Names ==","raw_wikitext":"{{Infobox Titan\n| image   = File:Bonelasher.jpg\n| attack  = 3\n| defense = 3\n| type    = [[Swara-Titan]] Warrior\n| size    = Medium\n| ability = Legendary Defender\n| users   = [[DeFoe]] <br> [[Gregor]] <br> [[Lee Roy]]<br>[[Suits]]<br>[[The Professor's Personal Guard]]<br>[[Unnamed Suit 026]]<br>[[Unnamed Suit 028]]<br>[[Unnamed Suit 029]]<br>[[Unnamed Suit 039]]<br>[[Unnamed Suit 040]]<br>[[Unnamed Suit 042]]<br>[[Unnamed Suit 055]]\n| height  = 8 feet 11 inches\n| weight  = 610 pounds\n| first   = \"[[Home Turf]]\"\n}}\n'''Bonelasher''' is the evolved cousin of [[Redcap]], the favored [[Titan]] of low-level [[The Organization|Organization]] Suits, but he is a bit stronger and harder to control. With the same aggression and passion for combat as his Titan relative, Bonelasher is best unleashed by his [[Seeker]] in the midst of a battle. With his army of razor-sharp claws and teeth, Bonelasher is best fought at distance.\n\n== History ==\nTwo Bonelasher Titans were summoned by [[The Professor's Personal Guard]] to fight [[Eathon Lambert]] in [[Atlantis]]. They were defeated by a combined attack from [[Dendras]] and [[Jirwolf]]. {{source|Coming of Age}}\n\nYears later, in [[Newgrange Passage Tomb]], Bonelasher was used by [[Klaus]]'s suits alongside [[Enforcer]]. One fought [[Caliban]] but was defeated. Later on, two defeated [[Lok Lambert]]'s [[Freelancer]] but were then taken out by [[Kilthane]] and [[Gybolg]]. {{Source|Home Turf}}\n\nBonelasher was used by [[Wilder]]'s Suits, alongside [[Venomaster]] and [[Gigadrone]] Titans, to pursue the Huntik team. One was defeated by being squashed under a tree levered by [[Dante Vale]]'s [[Dragonfist]] power. {{source|Knight of the Willblade}}\n\n== Abilities ==\nBonelasher can do massive amounts of damage with his fists. He is capable of punching through walls and Titans easily. He can stand amounts of damage most other Titans can't. With his razor-sharp claws and teeth, Bonelasher is best fought at a distance. Though Bonelasher is often paired with an [[Enforcer]] in battle, most of these Titans are preferred to be used independently.\n\n{{clear}}\n== Gallery ==\n{{gallery}}\n<gallery position=\"center\" captionalign=\"center\">\nBonelasher Amulet.jpg|Bonelasher's Amulet\nBonelasher Icon.jpg|Bonelasher's Icon\nBonelasher.jpg|Bonelasher\n</gallery>\n\n== Trivia ==\n*Bonelasher was originally named '''Ribbed Gremlin''', revealed in the storyboard animatic of \"[[The Bookshop Hunter]]\", included on DVD Journal 4 – ''The Professor Revealed'' (Anime Works / US Release). In folklore, Gremlins were mischievous spirits known to cause trouble and complications in machinery.  \n\n== International Names ==\n{{InternationalNamesSmall\n|FR = Griffosaure}}\n\n[[Category:Titans]]\n[[Category:Swara-Titans]]\n[[Category:Warrior Titans]]\n[[Category:Organization Titans]]\n[[Category:Medium Titans]]\n[[Category:Season 1 Titans]]\n[[Category:Season 2 Titans]]\n{{clear}}{{SwaraBox}}","categories":["Medium Titans","Organization Titans","Season 1 Titans","Season 2 Titans","Swara-Titans","Titans","Warrior Titans"],"links":[{"target_title":"Swara-Titan","label":"Swara-Titan","target_id":"huntik:page:2842","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Swara-Titan","status":"resolved","href":"#/categories?name=Swara-Titans"},{"target_title":"DeFoe","label":"DeFoe","target_id":"huntik:page:2048","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/DeFoe","status":"resolved","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A2048"},{"target_title":"Gregor","label":"Gregor","target_id":"huntik:page:8549","target